{% block brandDescription %}
      <p class="brand-description">Founded in 1931 by Adolph Rickenbacker and George Beauchamp in Los Angeles, Rickenbacker is the pioneer of the electric guitar industry, producing the first commercially successful electric guitars (the "Frying Pan" lap steel). Known for their jangly tone and distinctive cresting wave body shape, Rickenbacker guitars became iconic through artists like The Beatles, The Byrds, and Tom Petty. All Rickenbacker instruments are still handcrafted in Santa Ana, California, USA.<br><a href="#" class="decoder-howto-link" data-modal-target="howto-rickenbacker">(How to decode a Rickenbacker serial #)</a></p>
