{% block decoderNote %}
    <div class="decoder-note">
      <p>Note: Rickenbacker serial number formats have changed multiple times over the decades. Modern instruments (1999-present) use a YYWWNNN format. Earlier eras use letter codes for year and month. Pre-1954 serial numbers are not reliably datable. If you try a serial number and the decoder is not able to decode it, please <a href="../contact-us.html">contact us</a> and let us know so we can check the number and fix the decoder. Thank you!</p>
    </div>
{% endblock %}

{% block howtoModal %}
  <div id="howto-rickenbacker" class="decoder-modal hidden" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="howto-rickenbacker-title">
    <div class="decoder-modal-backdrop" data-modal-close></div>
    <div class="decoder-modal-content" role="document">
      <button type="button" class="decoder-modal-close" aria-label="Close dialog" data-modal-close>&times;</button>
      <div class="decoder-modal-header">
        <h2 id="howto-rickenbacker-title">How to decode a Rickenbacker serial number</h2>
        <p class="decoder-modal-subtitle">A quick manual method when you don't want to use a decoder.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="decoder-modal-body">
        <p>Rickenbacker guitar serial numbers, typically stamped on the metal jackplate, are decoded based on production era. Post‑1999 models use a 7‑digit code (YYWWPPL: Year, Week, Production Number). From 1987–1998, two letters indicate month/year, while 1961–1986 used a letter for year and another for month.</p>

        <h3>Modern System (1999–Present)</h3>
        <ul class="decoder-howto-steps">
          <li><strong>Format:</strong> 7 digits (e.g., 2135123)</li>
          <li><strong>Digits 1–2:</strong> Last two digits of the year (e.g., “21” = 2021).</li>
          <li><strong>Digits 3–4:</strong> Week of the year (01–52).</li>
          <li><strong>Digits 5–7:</strong> Production unit number.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>1987–1998 System</h3>
        <ul class="decoder-howto-steps">
          <li><strong>Format:</strong> Letter (Month) + Letter (Year) + 3 or 4 digits.</li>
          <li><strong>Month Letter:</strong> A=Jan, B=Feb, C=Mar, D=Apr, E=May, F=Jun, G=Jul, H=Aug, I=Sep, J=Oct, K=Nov, L=Dec.</li>
          <li><strong>Year Letter:</strong> Starts with A=1987, B=1988, etc.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>1961–1986 System</h3>
        <ul class="decoder-howto-steps">
          <li><strong>Format:</strong> Letter (Year) + Letter (Month) + 3 or 4 digits.</li>
          <li><strong>Year Letter:</strong> A=1961, B=1962, …, Z=1986 (Note: J can be 1960 or 1970).</li>
          <li><strong>Month Letter:</strong> A=Jan, B=Feb, …, L=Dec.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Key Tips</h3>
        <ul class="decoder-howto-steps">
          <li><strong>Location:</strong> Always on the metal output jack plate.</li>
          <li><strong>Exceptions:</strong> Some reissues (V‑series) or specialized models may follow different, older, or sequential numbering schemes.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
